  "implementation": [
    "Public DoubleMapNode<K1,K2> is a real repr(C) flat node: MapLinkNode,ManuallyDrop<K2>,ManuallyDrop<K1>,typed second-chain pointer. Small keys reuse native TListNode tail padding without borrowing a whole padded base.",
    "Four native const-reference/rvalue constructor combinations map to from_refs/from_key1_ref/from_key2_ref/new. Forwarding in-place Key2 construction maps to construct and construct_ref factory adapters. Allocation happens before either factory when allocate_with/allocate_ref is used.",
    "Existing shared map_payload constructs Key2 before Key1 and destroys Key1 before Key2. Key-copy failure drops the initialized second key. Rust destructor panics still run value cleanup and exact-layout deallocation through existing NativeNodeOwner/node_release.",
    "Key1 const and mutable native overloads map to key1 and change_key1. Key2 and inherited Value refer to the same actual field; ChangeValue edits that field. Next2 returns a mutable reference to the genuine typed pointer, while next2_value is a Rust shared-read adapter.",
    "Both links are non-owning. Raw deletion destroys and releases only the current node. First-link and second-link identities/mutation are independent; a custom test container stores actual nodes in real BaseDoubleMapStorage with opposite chain orders.",
    "BasicMapNode exposes primary bucket traversal and real payload projections. The exact native unordered KEY_ONLY specialization reads Key2 through Value for dereference, arrow and generic Key; it does not read Key1. No BasicMapNodeMut implementation permits generic writable keys.",
    "Raw node Send/Sync restrictions are retained; no new unsafe auto-trait implementation was added. Typed owner transfer preserves addresses and allocator identity. Mutable owner, constructor failures, key/value Drop panics, callback deletion, zero-sized payloads and aligned allocation pass Miri.",
    "Existing Rust NodeTrace and C++ NodeItem/NodeArena fixtures were extracted without changing their behavior, so DataMap and DoubleMap constructor/drop/allocation tests share named observers rather than duplicate instrumentation. The original DataMap11-row fixture remains unchanged in result.",
    "Ten direct visible native method declarations have scoped overload candidates recorded separately. Inherited Value/ChangeValue/Next are exercised through actual field projections and the generic iterator bridge. No global inventory credit is assigned."
